  ProjectName: DroneStrikeVR
  ClientName: CodeImpact
  Tags: 162
  Texts:
  - category: 0
    info: Unity Developer (Sole Developer)
  - category: 2
    info: 'A VR base-defence strategy game for Oculus Quest. Players protect their
      main tower from waves of enemy drones while attacking the opponent''s key infrastructure.



      Economy:
      an oil factory generates credits used to buy new assets. Credits carry over
      between levels.

      Defence: radar improves drone detection, air defence
      shoots down incoming threats, and handheld weapons let the player fight directly.

      Offence:
      precision-guided missiles and kamikaze drones target the enemy''s radar, oil
      factory and air defence. Destroying them wins the level.

      Progression:
      each level adds complexity and new weapons, and leaderboards score players
      on remaining oil and base damage.

      The project was stopped before the
      end of production.'
  - category: 3
    info: I was the only developer on a project of this scale. With many moving units
      and simultaneous AI behaviours, performance problems built up quickly on the
      Quest's mobile hardware.
  - category: 9
    info: '- Used Unity''s profiling tools to find CPU bottlenecks, memory spikes
      and inefficient update loops.

      - Reworked the offending systems, which
      improved both stability and overall frame rate on device.'
